NOTE ON SCOPE

This MIT licence covers the DisCanVisFlow pipeline code itself — the Nextflow
workflow (`main.nf`, `modules/`), the Python workers (`bin/`), the
configuration files (`config/`), and the documentation (`docs/`).

It does NOT cover the third-party reference data, databases, and prediction
tools that the pipeline downloads or invokes at runtime. Those carry their own
licences, several of which are non-commercial or require registration
(IUPred3/ANCHOR2, dbNSFP, COSMIC/CGC, OMIM, TCGA, AlphaMissense, FINCHES,
PhosphoSitePlus, ELM, BLAT, and others).

Using this pipeline does not grant you any rights to those resources. Before
using DisCanVisFlow — especially commercially — review CITATIONS.md, which
lists the licence and citation requirement of every data source and tool.
